oned regional languages and with Malay creoles; standard Indonesian is spoken in informal speech as a lingua franca between vernacular Malay dialects, Malay creoles, and regional languages. | Indonesian language - Wikipedia: Indonesian (Bahasa Indonesia) is the official and national language of Indonesia. [7] It is a standardized variety of Malay, [8] an Austronesian language that has been used as a lingua franca in the multilingual Indonesian archipelago for centuries. With over 280 million inhabitants, [9] Indonesia ranks as the fourth-most populous nation globally. | Bahasa Indonesia Book 1: Introduction to Indonesian Language and Culture (book): Bahasa Indonesia Book 1: Introduction to Indonesian Language and Culture is the first volume of a two-volume textbook series that delivers a structured, graded course in Bahasa Indonesia, the official language of Indonesia, while integrating aspects…
