[WEB SEARCH RESULT] Board game: A board game is a type of tabletop game that involves small objects (game pieces) that are placed and moved in particular ways on a specially designed patterned game board, potentially including other components, e.g. dice. The earliest known uses of the term "board game" are between the 1840s and 1850s.While game boards are a necessary and sufficient condition of this genre, card games that do not use a standard deck of cards, as well as games that use neither cards nor a game board, are often colloquially included, with some referring to this genre generally as "table and board games" or simply "tabletop games". | Board game: A board game is a non-digital tabletop game played by two or more participants who use physical pieces, such as counters, tokens, or figures, moved across a pre-marked board or surface... | Browse Board Games | BoardGameGeek: Board Games Artists Designers Publishers Accessories Families Forums GeekLists Honors Tags Wiki Users Podcasts Podcast Ep.Board Game: The Lord of the Rings: Duel for Middle-earth.
